 "notes": [
  "Validated at HEAD 12439ac5d9554282593820325466e82f356d726e (main after the merge of PR #3880). The study was committed in 98d68007c83909d9d9e1146b6973395421ab4dac. records.jsonl and plan.json moved to the artifact store in 92e900d6419a6ff095a5df9319f8bd3203dc360f; that commit also moved the report PNG. The local copies validated hash to sessions/main/.artifacts.json and to session.json records_sha256 / plan_sha256 (hashed_in_artifact_store). No other file under the study changed between 98d68007c83909d9d9e1146b6973395421ab4dac and HEAD. raw_data lists only files tracked in Git, with `path` relative to benchmarks/20261111-rho-chained-vs-v5v6 and `repo_path` repository-relative.",
  "Independence: validate_chained.py reads records.jsonl directly. It reuses, unchanged, the prime-field arithmetic and curve derivation of the validator's validate.py. No ecbench code is used. Both sources and their sha256 are embedded in replay-certificate.json. No keyring signature; no pcc claim registered by the validator.",
  "Filter: non-warmup records with outcome.status == 'verified' (1152 per arm). Every record's cost.s equals total_gae / sqrt(r), its phases' gae sum to total_gae, and its floor_s equals sqrt(pi / (2A)) with A = 2 (max errors 0). Pairs are matched by (workload_id, round) and share algorithm_seed and target; there are no duplicates and no unpaired records.",
  "Tolerances: rel_tol 0.002 for values printed to 3-4 significant figures. For the mechanism values printed to 1-2 significant figures (0.045, 0.003, 0.051, 0.046), rel_tol is half a unit in the last printed place divided by the claim, so each passes exactly when the recomputed value rounds to it: 0.04468, 0.00286, 0.05147 and 0.04554 all round correctly. These are low-precision claims; the recomputed values are in the headline list.",
  "Finding, unpriced work not declared: chained, chained-aa and legacy run distinguished-point walks (104755 and 68939 distinguished points over 1152 runs; their work blocks list one hash_probe each). But their cost.unpriced names only canonicalisations_uncharged, while v5 and v6 declare their distinguished-point table inserts and queries. The band as defined therefore charges v5/v6 for table work and not chained/legacy. Sensitivity, charging every arm's table work at w = 1 (one op per hash probe / two per distinguished point): v5/chained 0.2596 / 0.2582 (declared 0.2610); chained/legacy 3.4019 / 3.3807 (declared 3.4236); v5/legacy 0.8832 / 0.8730 (declared 0.8937). Every order holds at every weight in every variant, so no ranking changes. The declared-counter band, however, is not 'every arm priced' in the section 5a sense for chained and legacy.",
  "Finding, REPORT.md prose: run-20261111T0324Z/REPORT.md says v5's walk 'records no cycle'. 270 of 1152 non-warmup v5 records detect cycles (621 cycles, 621 escape doublings; mean 0.000426 per sqrt(r)). The report's table value 0.000 is a correct 3-decimal rounding; the sentence is not supported. v6: 321 records, 853 doublings.",
  "Scope disclosure (observation): each pooled ratio is a ratio of mean S with equal weight per curve. chained/legacy per curve rises from 1.75 (2^17.7) to 7.62 (2^28.0); its summed total GAE ratio is 5.352. v5/chained per curve falls from 0.429 to 0.125; summed-GAE ratio 0.168. v5/legacy per curve runs from 0.751 to 0.953; summed-GAE ratio 0.901. The chained arm's walk_operations per sqrt(r) is 7.22 at 2^28 against 2.3-3.4 below it. Not headline: v6/v5 = 1.0225.",
  "Controls: chained-aa / chained is exactly 1.0. legacy rho.negation is the unmodified negation-map baseline. All six curves have j not in {0, 1728} and A = 2, so negation is the full automorphism group.",
  "Source binding: session.json records git_commit c7c4c2874f8a03b83b584041eff2fd5a1435ade0 (git_dirty false, an ancestor of HEAD) and binary 55289451c555.... audit.json replayed 5760 of 5760 non-warmup records 'identical' with the same binary and env class ECBENV3h0a8f39be1123 as the session. Its hardware class ECBHW1h0832b230440b cannot be compared, because host.json records no hardware class, so a cross-host replay is not established.",
  "L0 isolation: counted GAE only; no wall-clock figure is validated.",
  "Curve parameters: (a, b) were derived from G and a target point, then bound by the ICV1 model12 hash, the slug, j, the trace, docs/curves/registry.json, [r]G = O with r prime, and cofactor 1 from the Hasse bound (replay-certificate.json curve_parameters).",
  "m=83 / ECC2K-130: not applicable; rho measurements on prime curves of 18-28 bits; no transfer claim.",
  "The validator writes no VALIDATION.json."
